   // - @battle-movement-system.mdc#Attack-Range-Behavior#Range-Updates
   
   - Battalion Stats (from @DigitalBarracksScreen.tsx):
     - Fixed Per-Unit Stats:
       - Guardian: {speed: 9, range: 4, offense: 8, defense: 6, health: 14}
       - Phreak: {speed: 7, range: 9, offense: 6, defense: 5, health: 12}
       - Breacher: {speed: 5, range: 5, offense: 7, defense: 8, health: 18}
     
     - Scaling Stats (Backend Calculated):
       - Total Health = base_health * battalion_quantity
       - Total Attack = base_offense * battalion_quantity
       
     - Fixed Stats (Frontend Used):
       - Movement Speed = base_speed (unchanged by quantity)
       - Attack Range = base_range (unchanged by quantity)
       - Defense = base_defense (as % damage reduction)
     
     - Combat Calculations (Backend Only):
       - Incoming Damage = attacker_total_attack * (1 - defender_defense/100)
       - Minimum Damage = 1 (ensure damage is never reduced to 0)
       - Attack Frequency = 1/base_speed attacks per second
       - Range Check = target_distance <= base_range

   - Universal targeting rules:
     - ONLY factor is proximity to target
     - NO type-specific targeting preferences
     - Must be reachable via network lines
     - Target changes ONLY when proximity changes

   - State Management:
     Frontend Handles:
     - Target selection (proximity-based)
     - Movement calculation
     - Range checking
     - Visual feedback
     
     Backend Handles (1s updates):
     - Combat calculations
     - Health tracking
     - Damage resolution
     - State persistence

   - Health tracking per battalion
   - Universal capture mechanics:
     - Capture threshold = total battalion health * 0.75
     - Damage accumulates towards control
     - Must overcome enemy control damage
     - All battalion types deal equal node damage

3. Error Prevention
   - Validate state before updates
   - Clear error logging
   - Simple recovery paths 